WEBVTT

00:34.220 --> 00:36.521
We now return to The Last Man on Earth

00:36.554 --> 00:39.590
Plus These Other 16 People with
More Showing Up Every Day.

00:39.623 --> 00:41.341
No way they'll pull this off.

00:41.343 --> 00:43.049
A show with just one character

00:43.051 --> 00:45.021
and an unlimited number
of other characters?

00:45.023 --> 00:47.757
Peter, you can't just sit
there and watch TV all day.

00:47.790 --> 00:50.027
- You have to mow the lawn.
- Aw, this sucks.

00:50.060 --> 00:51.767
I was gonna go down
to the Guitar Center

00:51.800 --> 00:52.905
and annoy people.

01:00.563 --> 01:04.615
FYI: My mom's not picking me
up for a long time, because...

01:07.172 --> 01:08.543
she's dead!

01:12.102 --> 01:13.571
Hey, Brian, you want a beer?

01:13.605 --> 01:15.243
Peter, Lois is gonna be home soon.

01:15.275 --> 01:16.689
Shouldn't you be mowing the lawn?

01:16.722 --> 01:18.239
I am mowing the lawn.

01:20.834 --> 01:22.822
- Where'd you get these?
- Craigslist.

01:22.855 --> 01:25.357
Boy, that's got to be some long list.

01:25.391 --> 01:28.060
And pool tables and jukeboxes...

01:28.093 --> 01:30.059
Craig, are you getting all this down?

01:30.092 --> 01:31.560
Yes. Is that it?

01:31.593 --> 01:35.596
No! Futons, everyone's
grandfather's golf clubs...

01:35.630 --> 01:36.729
I-Is that it?

01:36.763 --> 01:38.431
No! Gay sex...

01:38.464 --> 01:40.632
- What kind?
- All of it!

01:44.769 --> 01:46.904
I have milked all the goats.

01:46.906 --> 01:48.908
Peter, all those goats are males.

01:48.910 --> 01:51.512
Well, the buckets are full
and the goats are happy.

01:51.544 --> 01:53.744
I just hope word doesn't get around.

01:54.978 --> 01:57.014
I like good times.

02:00.683 --> 02:02.651
We now return to Top Gun

02:02.683 --> 02:04.651
with only public domain music.

02:13.354 --> 02:16.824
Oh, my God, what the hell
did the goats do in here?

02:16.858 --> 02:18.323
This place is disgusting!

02:18.357 --> 02:19.692
Where's your father?

02:19.725 --> 02:20.860
Peter!

02:28.396 --> 02:30.463
Lois is maaaad.

02:30.496 --> 02:32.631
Go to the Claaaam.

02:32.665 --> 02:36.034
Peter, I both saw you and
recognized my husband's voice.

02:36.066 --> 02:37.902
Go baaaack.

02:39.703 --> 02:41.503
Lois! I-I didn't know you were home.

02:41.537 --> 02:45.138
Well, I guess we can all agree
this was a great idea. The end.

02:47.238 --> 02:49.473
Enough! My parents will
be here any minute.

02:49.507 --> 02:51.475
You better get this house cleaned up.

02:51.509 --> 02:53.644
Don't worry, Lois. I have a Roomba.

02:57.110 --> 02:58.712
Okay, wait, wait, wait a minute.

02:58.744 --> 03:00.712
It'll... it'll figure it out.

03:00.746 --> 03:03.348
It's learning. That's-that's
part of what it does.

03:03.380 --> 03:05.248
I think it's getting it.

03:05.282 --> 03:07.181
Now she's cookin'.

03:07.214 --> 03:09.416
Hang on to your hat.

03:09.450 --> 03:11.919
Clean floor dead ahead.

03:11.951 --> 03:13.819
Good purchase.

03:13.852 --> 03:15.820
Behold the future.

03:15.854 --> 03:17.389
All right, here it goes.

03:18.622 --> 03:19.988
And the battery's dead.

03:22.724 --> 03:24.892
Darling, so wonderful to be here.

03:24.925 --> 03:27.227
Yeah, right. The drive here is like

03:27.259 --> 03:29.894
a counterclockwise trip
around the Monopoly board.

03:29.928 --> 03:32.428
He has no paaaants.

03:32.462 --> 03:34.297
Peter, get out of there.

03:36.063 --> 03:37.898
Lois, what's going on here?

03:37.932 --> 03:40.234
Well, I asked Peter to mow the lawn.

03:40.266 --> 03:42.389
Will somebody turn off Top Gun?!

03:43.451 --> 03:45.002
So obviously he bought a herd of goats,

03:45.035 --> 03:47.070
and now they've taken over the house.

03:47.102 --> 03:49.671
Lois, I worry this is not
a healthy environment

03:49.705 --> 03:51.573
- for the children.
- Mom, please.

03:51.605 --> 03:54.240
You know I would never put
my children in harm's way.

03:54.274 --> 03:55.739
Oh, boy. AMBER Alert.

03:55.773 --> 03:58.608
Stewie was last seen with a
goat in a '98 Toyota Tercel

03:58.642 --> 04:00.010
heading north on I-95.

04:00.042 --> 04:01.945
How do you turn those off, by the way?

04:01.977 --> 04:03.578
Lois, I've seen enough.

04:03.612 --> 04:07.014
You're completely overwhelmed,
and you have four children.

04:07.047 --> 04:09.247
Four children.

04:09.280 --> 04:11.448
Four children.

04:11.481 --> 04:13.547
Four children.

04:13.580 --> 04:15.867
Four children.

04:15.900 --> 04:17.952
Four children.

04:17.985 --> 04:19.353
Hey!

04:19.387 --> 04:20.752
You need help, Lois.

04:20.786 --> 04:22.754
And since I don't believe in psychiatry,

04:22.787 --> 04:24.769
I'm getting you a nanny.

04:24.803 --> 04:26.457
Well, I guess it would be
good to have some help

04:26.489 --> 04:27.548
with Meg and Chris.

04:27.582 --> 04:29.625
And Stewie, if he's ever found.

04:32.258 --> 04:34.527
Honey, do you think
that's the goat and baby

04:34.560 --> 04:37.028
- from the AMBER alert?
- Uh, it's a Tercel,

04:37.060 --> 04:39.663
but I don't think it's the right year.

04:46.833 --> 04:48.568
That must be the new nanny.

04:48.600 --> 04:50.568
Is this the Griffin house?

04:50.601 --> 04:52.971
Welcome to this work environment.

04:53.004 --> 04:55.372
Oh. I'm not the nanny.
I'm her Uber driver.

04:55.405 --> 04:56.938
Your nanny's still in the car.

04:56.970 --> 04:58.738
She dozed off on the way here.

04:58.772 --> 05:00.741
I not doze off, Yoober.

05:00.774 --> 05:03.985
Was looking at crinkled
photos of dead relatives.

05:04.017 --> 05:05.576
Hello. I am Natalia.

05:05.609 --> 05:07.811
What is favorite breakfast fish?

05:07.844 --> 05:09.944
Well, if you must know...

05:09.978 --> 05:13.314
Welcome to this work environment.

05:19.852 --> 05:21.485
Okay, Natalia, level with me.

05:21.518 --> 05:22.853
Why are you really here?

05:22.886 --> 05:25.921
I have been sent to neutralize
liberal Jewish dissident,

05:25.954 --> 05:27.824
Fievel Mousekewitz.

05:29.857 --> 05:31.993
Oh. Well, the only mouse
in this neighborhood is

05:32.026 --> 05:34.026
our innocent neighbor, Frank Maxwell.

05:35.358 --> 05:37.190
Comrade Mousekewitz!

05:37.223 --> 05:39.362
Did you think you could run forever?

05:39.395 --> 05:42.197
I, uh, I think you've
got the wrong mouse.

05:42.231 --> 05:44.665
I'm just regular old Frank Maxwell,

05:44.698 --> 05:46.833
and I'm very late for work.

05:46.865 --> 05:48.366
Good day, ma'am.

05:50.567 --> 05:52.535
Whoa! You killed him?

05:52.568 --> 05:53.936
That was not me.

05:53.970 --> 05:55.838
Someone else got to him first.

05:56.837 --> 05:59.015
Tough break, Jew mouse. Ha-ha!

05:59.734 --> 06:01.006
Hi. I'm Peter Griffin.

06:01.040 --> 06:03.842
Under parody law, in order to
use someone else's character

06:03.874 --> 06:06.142
in an unlicensed fashion,
we have to provide

06:06.175 --> 06:07.710
something called "commentary."

06:07.742 --> 06:10.777
The commentary here is that
Mickey Mouse hates Jews.

06:10.810 --> 06:14.646
Now, let's see what else this
new nanny has up her sleeve.

06:18.583 --> 06:21.983
Okay, Stewie, this is favorite
Belarusian children book

06:22.015 --> 06:25.318
called Goodnight Moon of Chernobyl.

06:25.351 --> 06:27.386
"Goodnight Chernobyl moon.

06:27.419 --> 06:30.042
Goodnight radiation house.

06:30.074 --> 06:32.189
Goodnight melted phone.

06:32.222 --> 06:34.456
Goodnight glowing milk.

06:34.489 --> 06:37.392
Goodnight bleeding grandpa's eyes.

06:37.424 --> 06:39.859
Goodnight two-headed cat.

06:39.892 --> 06:42.028
Goodnight nobody.

06:42.061 --> 06:45.962
Goodnight blocks and blocks
and blocks of nobody.

06:45.994 --> 06:47.796
The end."

06:47.830 --> 06:49.398
Next book.

06:49.430 --> 06:51.198
Everybody Poops...

06:51.232 --> 06:53.001
Blood.

06:56.801 --> 06:58.936
I'll get started on dinner.

07:01.102 --> 07:02.571
No need to start dinner.

07:02.604 --> 07:04.905
Homework is done. Kids are fed.

07:04.938 --> 07:07.430
You two should go out and
have lovely evening.

07:07.490 --> 07:10.624
- Together?
- Yes. Everything taken care of.

07:10.656 --> 07:13.253
Go out. Enjoy American freedom.

07:13.286 --> 07:14.566
What do you say, Peter?

07:14.599 --> 07:16.794
Eh, it could be fun. And
we haven't been on a date

07:16.827 --> 07:18.161
since I broke the Guinness record

07:18.194 --> 07:20.904
for longest nasal exhale
at that Tina Fey movie.

07:20.938 --> 07:23.965
You're the baby mama?
Well, that's no bueno.

07:39.006 --> 07:40.106
Hello. I'm Steve.

07:40.139 --> 07:41.641
I'll be your server this evening.

07:41.673 --> 07:43.312
May I start you off with a cocktail?

07:46.510 --> 07:47.909
You don't work here, do you?

07:47.943 --> 07:49.163
I do not.

07:49.843 --> 07:51.478
Oh, this is nice.

07:51.512 --> 07:53.147
So, how's work?

07:53.179 --> 07:54.647
Good.

07:56.349 --> 07:57.816
How, uh...

07:57.848 --> 08:00.082
how's the stuff you
do during your day?

08:00.115 --> 08:01.783
- Good.
- Good.

08:03.018 --> 08:04.651
So... is that it?

08:04.685 --> 08:07.321
Did we do a date? Phones back on?

08:07.354 --> 08:09.622
Peter, we finally have
a chance to reconnect.

08:09.654 --> 08:11.188
We've been given this opportunity.

08:11.220 --> 08:12.789
It's like before we had kids.

08:12.823 --> 08:14.691
We got to make the most of it.

08:14.724 --> 08:16.024
H-Hang on, hang on, Lois.

08:16.056 --> 08:18.427
Give me two of those round balls
of butter and a breadstick.

08:18.459 --> 08:19.859
You'll see where I'm
heading with this.

08:19.892 --> 08:22.996
Okay, look, look, look.
Here's what you want.

08:23.029 --> 08:24.996
Here's what you got.

08:25.028 --> 08:27.163
I'm very happy with what I got.

08:27.196 --> 08:31.056
Hmm. Well, maybe I can give
you half a breadstick later.

08:31.089 --> 08:34.268
As long as you don't mind a
little marinara dipping sauce.

08:34.300 --> 08:36.527
That's absolutely disgusting.

08:36.560 --> 08:37.835
And I love it.

08:37.868 --> 08:40.338
You know what? I like date night.

08:40.371 --> 08:42.506
To Natalia, for making it possible.

08:43.638 --> 08:45.640
Pretty sure that's Steve's pee.

08:45.672 --> 08:47.298
Enjoying your wine?

08:52.909 --> 08:55.180
Oh, what an amazing night.

08:55.212 --> 08:58.179
I told you we could have a fun
time, just the two of us.

08:58.213 --> 09:00.180
Fun's not over yet.

09:01.895 --> 09:03.381
Come on, let's get in the trunk.

09:03.414 --> 09:06.350
I filled it with water so
we can do it hippo-style.

09:06.383 --> 09:07.684
Weightlessly,

09:07.717 --> 09:10.352
with my feet lightly scraping
the bottom as we do it.

09:10.386 --> 09:12.653
Okay. It's kind of sexy, I guess.

09:12.686 --> 09:14.520
And in the hippo tradition,

09:14.552 --> 09:16.855
first we must eat a
whole head of lettuce.

09:16.888 --> 09:20.724
- Now, do you have the lettuce?
- I-I didn't know we were doing this.

09:20.757 --> 09:22.358
Did you bring the lettuce?

09:22.391 --> 09:23.693
Oh, no, I forgot.

09:23.726 --> 09:25.859
Ronald, I asked you to do one thing.

09:25.893 --> 09:28.395
Honey, honey... I brought the lettuce.

09:33.597 --> 09:34.997
So thanks to Natalia,

09:35.031 --> 09:37.199
we've been spending so
much more time together.

09:37.232 --> 09:39.667
Let me tell you, Joe, it's
really been a rediscovery.

09:39.699 --> 09:41.741
- Hmm.
- Joe, "we time"

09:41.775 --> 09:44.610
- is just as important as "me time."
- Okay.

09:44.704 --> 09:46.970
We've actually been watching
The Middle together.

09:47.003 --> 09:50.014
It's so funny! Isn't it funny, Peter?

09:50.047 --> 09:52.039
It is actually funny. At
least three times an episode

09:52.072 --> 09:54.041
we turn to each other and we say,

09:54.074 --> 09:55.743
"That's just like us!"

09:57.243 --> 09:58.577
Why are you laughing?

09:58.609 --> 10:01.076
- It sounded funny.
- But you had to be there.

10:01.110 --> 10:03.412
Well, I was able to
imagine myself there,

10:03.445 --> 10:05.147
which is why I chuckled.

10:05.180 --> 10:07.482
Oh, and, Donna, have you
seen this Black-ish?

10:07.515 --> 10:09.549
- Why are you asking me that?
- I don't know.

10:09.582 --> 10:11.649
It seems like you might like it.

10:11.683 --> 10:14.925
Oh, and, waiter, have you
seen this Fresh Off the Boat?

10:14.958 --> 10:16.853
- Why are you asking me that?
- I don't know.

10:16.886 --> 10:18.553
It seems like you might like it.

10:18.586 --> 10:19.755
Oh, there's Mort. Mort!

10:19.788 --> 10:22.223
Have you seen this The Goldbergs?

10:22.255 --> 10:24.643
Yes! I like it 'cause I'm Jewish.

10:27.790 --> 10:30.811
Boy, our friends all seem
to be happily married.

10:31.760 --> 10:33.695
Yeah, right.

10:33.728 --> 10:35.362
You know, Donna told
me in the bathroom

10:35.394 --> 10:37.063
she and Cleveland haven't had sex

10:37.096 --> 10:38.229
in over three months.

10:38.262 --> 10:39.430
I love that you share things

10:39.463 --> 10:41.164
that were told to you in confidence.

10:41.197 --> 10:43.666
- Oh, and the poor Swansons.
- I know.

10:43.699 --> 10:45.167
Joe's dead from the waist down,

10:45.200 --> 10:46.734
and Bonnie's dead from the waist up.

10:46.767 --> 10:48.102
They're perfect for each other.

10:48.135 --> 10:50.603
I know, I know.

10:50.635 --> 10:52.569
I got to say, Peter,
I really feel like

10:52.603 --> 10:54.406
Natalia has helped put the spark back

10:54.438 --> 10:55.873
in our relationship.

10:55.906 --> 10:58.280
Yeah, we even had
independent movie sex.

10:59.177 --> 11:02.341
I want to lean over this
half-eaten blueberry pie

11:02.374 --> 11:04.575
and kiss you with black coffee breath.

11:04.608 --> 11:06.263
- Is that okay?
- Yes.

11:09.779 --> 11:12.181
Now, can I do you to a song you know,

11:12.214 --> 11:13.616
but sung in German?

11:27.954 --> 11:31.389
Hello? I see.

11:31.422 --> 11:32.672
What is it?

11:32.705 --> 11:34.485
I've been assassinated.

11:43.963 --> 11:45.898
Wow, what a night.

11:45.930 --> 11:49.199
I guess someone's sleep number is 69.

11:49.232 --> 11:52.600
Uh, yes. It was, apparently,
also number two.

11:52.633 --> 11:55.051
Would you maybe make some
coffee and give me a moment?

11:55.968 --> 11:58.203
Car is packed for weekend.

11:58.236 --> 11:59.539
- Weekend?
- Yes.

11:59.572 --> 12:01.206
You come in late last night drunk

12:01.239 --> 12:03.740
and tell me to pack car
for weekend getaway

12:03.772 --> 12:05.041
you book online.

12:05.074 --> 12:08.042
Then you make me watch
Diff'rent Strokes episode

12:08.074 --> 12:11.713
with substitute teacher played
by Kareem Abdul-Jabbar.

12:12.444 --> 12:14.313
You know, I forgot about
this weekend trip.

12:14.345 --> 12:16.280
I-Is that something
we still want to do?

12:16.313 --> 12:17.813
Well, I do if you do.

12:17.846 --> 12:20.047
Absolutely I do... I-I was
just seeing if you do.

12:20.081 --> 12:21.649
Of course I do.

12:21.682 --> 12:24.250
I mean, we've already had
six nights out together.

12:24.283 --> 12:26.247
It'd be great to have three more.

12:26.280 --> 12:27.284
That's what I'm saying.

12:27.317 --> 12:28.819
That-That's what any guy wants,

12:28.852 --> 12:31.587
the same gal again and again and again

12:31.620 --> 12:33.955
and again and again
and again and again

12:33.988 --> 12:36.458
and again and again
and again and again

12:36.491 --> 12:38.392
and again and again, and again.

12:38.424 --> 12:40.758
And every gal wants the
same guy who keeps

12:40.792 --> 12:43.426
getting fatter and fatter
and fatter and fatter...

12:43.459 --> 12:45.261
Stop it right there, Lois.
This is Family Guy.

12:45.294 --> 12:47.328
We only do the male side of the joke.

12:48.304 --> 12:51.065
You know what? I think
this weekend will be fun.

12:51.097 --> 12:52.430
Yeah. I mean, it's
not like we're gonna

12:52.464 --> 12:53.964
miss anything around here.

12:58.367 --> 12:59.901
Hey, Joe, what the
hell's going on here?

12:59.935 --> 13:02.103
Oh, you didn't hear?
Today is the opening

13:02.136 --> 13:05.270
of the first-ever Spooner
Street Farmers Market.

13:05.304 --> 13:07.939
Farmers...

13:07.972 --> 13:10.640
market?

13:10.673 --> 13:12.308
Yeah, it's really exciting.

13:12.341 --> 13:14.442
For 50 cents, you can
get your picture taken

13:14.476 --> 13:16.143
wearing a farmer's hat.

13:16.176 --> 13:19.145
Farmer's...

13:19.177 --> 13:21.512
hat?

13:21.546 --> 13:23.481
Hey, have a great weekend, you two.

13:23.513 --> 13:26.849
So glad you're finding
time for each other.

13:30.550 --> 13:31.818
Goat meat.

13:31.850 --> 13:33.485
Get your goat meat here.

13:33.519 --> 13:34.987
- Cleveland, are those...
- Yep.

13:35.020 --> 13:36.821
I have dibs on whatever silliness

13:36.853 --> 13:38.521
Peter loses interest in.

13:38.554 --> 13:39.689
Remember this?

13:39.722 --> 13:41.856
To the Cleveland copter!

13:43.823 --> 13:45.924
The moustache obscures my view!

13:55.337 --> 13:56.739
Oh, another hawk.

13:56.773 --> 13:58.107
Or maybe it's the same one.

13:58.140 --> 13:59.608
You think it could be the same one?

13:59.640 --> 14:00.695
Doubt it.

14:01.508 --> 14:02.775
Hey, do you have the address?

14:02.808 --> 14:04.609
I think it's in my
pocketbook somewhere.

14:04.642 --> 14:07.144
'Cause I got to know if
we should take 24 or 495.

14:07.176 --> 14:08.522
Hang on.

14:09.645 --> 14:11.674
- Anything?
- Hang on.

14:12.716 --> 14:14.050
Exit's coming up.

14:15.182 --> 14:16.610
Half a mile.

14:19.283 --> 14:20.652
Quarter mile.

14:20.684 --> 14:21.952
You'd think I could find it.

14:21.985 --> 14:23.320
Yeah, yeah, I would.

14:23.352 --> 14:26.087
I would. Okay, I'm taking 495.

14:26.120 --> 14:28.222
Okay, uh, here, let me see if it's...

14:28.256 --> 14:31.291
Oh, this is why I don't
like big purses.

14:31.322 --> 14:34.758
Here it is. It says take 24 to 128.

14:55.335 --> 14:56.670
Hey, look, cookies.

14:56.703 --> 14:58.471
- Chocolate chip?
- Oatmeal raisin.

15:00.137 --> 15:03.506
Ah, I guess they stopped
serving dinner at 9:30.

15:03.539 --> 15:06.106
Looks like that missed
exit had the last laugh.

15:06.140 --> 15:07.409
Oh, look at this cute note.

15:07.441 --> 15:08.641
"In lieu of television,

15:08.674 --> 15:10.742
please tune in to each other."

15:10.775 --> 15:14.011
- Ha-ha.
- Ha-ha, indeed. And get this.

15:14.044 --> 15:16.146
"Sorry no Wi-Fi, but the good news is

15:16.180 --> 15:17.947
your marriage has four bars."

15:17.980 --> 15:20.347
- Terrific.
- Oh, here's another note.

15:20.380 --> 15:22.515
"How adorable were
those first two notes?

15:22.548 --> 15:24.250
I hope you read this one third."

15:24.283 --> 15:26.485
There's a used condom
in the fireplace.

15:26.518 --> 15:27.952
And the fireplace is decorative,

15:27.986 --> 15:29.154
so that's here to stay.

15:29.186 --> 15:30.652
So, do you think word just got out

15:30.686 --> 15:32.254
in the daddy longlegs community, like,

15:32.287 --> 15:33.655
"Hey, come to this hotel"?

15:33.687 --> 15:35.121
Peter, it's a little warm in here.

15:35.155 --> 15:37.457
Do you want to turn on
that overhead ceiling fan?

15:37.490 --> 15:38.625
Sure. Looks stable.

15:41.693 --> 15:43.494
- Can you notice that?
- Yeah.

15:43.527 --> 15:45.695
Can you notice anything in
the world other than that?

15:45.728 --> 15:48.963
Only that fist-sized moth in
the lampshade by the bed.

15:48.997 --> 15:52.032
I'm going to bed so that "go
home time" comes faster.

16:03.088 --> 16:05.158
I'll just sleep with the light on.

16:10.506 --> 16:13.009
Natalia, will you be
our nanny forever?

16:13.042 --> 16:15.209
Dah, unless Belarus security force

16:15.243 --> 16:17.344
- track me down.
- I'm sorry, what?

16:17.377 --> 16:19.178
Natalia make a few enemies

16:19.211 --> 16:21.480
before she leave Belarus.

16:29.150 --> 16:31.884
Natalia save baby.

16:36.086 --> 16:38.355
- Brian?
- Lock door.

16:38.388 --> 16:39.389
Why would I...

16:39.422 --> 16:40.723
Brian!

16:44.223 --> 16:45.725
No kissing. Under bed.

16:55.495 --> 16:58.731
Aah!

17:03.034 --> 17:04.536
Out.

17:07.267 --> 17:08.536
Boy, that was a close one.

17:08.570 --> 17:10.571
Ah, my son was in the backseat.

17:58.961 --> 18:00.263
Daddy?

18:09.567 --> 18:10.733
Where are we going?

18:10.766 --> 18:12.168
You're going home.

18:12.202 --> 18:14.071
Count to three and pull cord.

18:16.270 --> 18:19.374
I don't know my numbers!

18:26.656 --> 18:28.362
Again! Again!

18:36.948 --> 18:38.849
- Oh. This.
- What?

18:38.882 --> 18:40.383
That mealy-mouth thing you do.

18:40.415 --> 18:41.517
Take a sip of water.

18:41.550 --> 18:43.184
I don't like water. I like pop.

18:43.218 --> 18:44.784
Hey, will you let me
know when you're done

18:44.818 --> 18:46.420
using the phone charger
that I brought?

18:46.453 --> 18:48.087
Oh, you mean the only
thing that you packed?

18:48.119 --> 18:49.753
Yeah, I just assumed if you pay,

18:49.787 --> 18:51.423
- you don't have to pack.
- Here we go.

18:51.455 --> 18:52.755
My husband, the Rockefeller,

18:52.789 --> 18:54.757
letting my parents pay for the nanny.

18:54.789 --> 18:56.259
Kids still lining up around the block

18:56.291 --> 18:57.557
for those piano lessons?

18:57.591 --> 18:59.093
I wonder which has more clutter on it,

18:59.125 --> 19:00.392
the piano or your treadmill.

19:00.425 --> 19:01.794
You know what? I'm gonna
go with the treadmill.

19:01.826 --> 19:04.394
Really? Let's go knock on
the door of the next room

19:04.428 --> 19:06.229
and ask them which one of us is fat.

19:06.263 --> 19:08.565
Oh, I'm so sorry I'm
not Bradley Hooper.

19:08.598 --> 19:09.864
It's Cooper, not Hooper.

19:09.897 --> 19:12.031
You're thinking of Mr.
Hooper from Sesame Street,

19:12.065 --> 19:13.367
and I'd sooner bang him.

19:13.399 --> 19:15.801
He was a business owner.
He was a successful man.

19:15.835 --> 19:17.702
You think you're the only
one in this relationship

19:17.736 --> 19:19.303
who wants to be with a successful man?

19:19.335 --> 19:20.346
Get over yourself.

19:20.347 --> 19:21.804
Oh, hey, do you want these
spit droplets back,

19:21.836 --> 19:23.104
Or are they for my arm to keep?

19:23.138 --> 19:25.406
Sorry, I was trying to scare
that fly on your hand.

19:25.438 --> 19:26.806
Oh, it's a liver spot. Never mind.

19:26.840 --> 19:29.324
I'm hoping it's cancer.
I want the ticket out.

19:29.357 --> 19:31.309
Oh, if you die, can I
have all of your nothing?

19:31.341 --> 19:32.776
What do you mean if I die?

19:32.810 --> 19:35.144
I've been dead since the
minute I said "I do"!

19:35.176 --> 19:36.611
Well, the minute you say "I don't,"

19:36.644 --> 19:37.878
I am out that door.

19:37.912 --> 19:40.480
- Oh, is that right?
- Yep.

19:40.514 --> 19:42.782
Well, what if I just said,
"The hell with it, go"?

19:42.814 --> 19:43.965
What if you did?

19:45.486 --> 19:46.616
Go.

19:46.991 --> 19:48.343
Fine!

20:42.678 --> 20:44.280
So, how was the trip?

20:48.242 --> 20:52.306
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru

20:52.683 --> 20:53.719
Just terrible.